title: June 2021

@opposition_reset
# prose-audit: Grade A — KO, Poland 2050 and Lewica compete through social, democratic and local strategies with distinct organisational aftermaths.
title: The opposition resets
face-image: img/poland/events/sejm-chamber.webp
new-page: true
on-arrival: opposition_reset_event_done = 1; news_headline = "KO and Poland 2050 contest the same centre"

= June 2021 — Three opposition strategies

KO asks every opposition party to line up behind a single anti-PiS pole.
Szymon Hołownia presents Poland 2050 as an escape from the habits of the old
opposition and courts voters who want a new centre. Our organisers hear both
pitches as an invitation to become somebody else's left flank.

The choice is not whether to oppose PiS. It is where we intend to remain
distinct while doing it.

- @reset_social
- @reset_democratic
- @reset_local

@reset_social
title: Compete with both on wages, housing and services
on-arrival: opposition_reset_strategy = "Social competition"; labor_credibility += 5; workers_support += 3; public_sector_support += 2; ko_relation -= 3; p2050_relation -= 3; left_economic_position -= 2; news_headline = "Lewica opens a social flank against both centrist parties"

Our MPs take wages, rents and public services on tour while KO and Poland 2050
compete over who can best manage the centre. Both accuse us of dividing the
opposition. Trade unionists and tenants' groups hear something rarer: a reason
to support the Left that is not merely fear of PiS.

- @dworczyk_hack_2021: Turn to the leaked mailbox


@reset_democratic
title: Rebuild the democratic-opposition table
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Requires one resource.
on-arrival: opposition_reset_strategy = "Democratic opposition table"; resources -= 1; ko_relation += 5; p2050_relation += 5; relation_ko_p2050 += 4; rival_relation_ko_p2050 += 4; constitutional_restraint += 3; razem_dissent += 3; news_headline = "The opposition table returns with written limits"

Lawyers and parliamentary whips sit down to agree on constitutional red lines,
procedural warnings and the votes on which nobody will surprise the others.
The table gives the opposition discipline without pretending it has one
programme. Razem still fears that every shared photograph teaches voters to
see us as a junior partner in somebody else's coalition.

- @dworczyk_hack_2021: Turn to the leaked mailbox


@reset_local
title: Leave Warsaw to the leaders and organise counties
on-arrival: opposition_reset_strategy = "County organisation"; local_network += 5; rural_support += 3; psl_relation += 3; media_capacity -= 1; news_headline = "County organisation replaces another leaders' summit"

The next Warsaw summit takes place without us. Our money goes instead to county
offices, bus-stop meetings and organisers looking for credible local
candidates. It produces fewer evening headlines, but more people know whom to
call when a clinic closes. PSL notices that the Left has begun treating the
counties as political ground rather than scenery between cities.

- @dworczyk_hack_2021: Turn to the leaked mailbox




@dworczyk_hack_2021
# prose-audit: Grade C — The mailbox, the government's non-denial and the choice between using and refusing stolen material are staged with a locked joint-committee route; the officials whose private correspondence is circulating remain a category.
title: The minister's mailbox
subtitle: Government business appears on Telegram and nobody will say what is genuine
face-image: img/poland/events/chancellery-2022.webp
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.dworczyk_hack_2021_done = 1;
Q.pis_poll_momentum = (Number(Q.pis_poll_momentum) || 0) - 0.45;
Q.russian_influence_salience =
    (Number(Q.russian_influence_salience) || 0) + 10;
Q.institutional_trust = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) - 5
);
Q.infosec_exposure =
    (Number(Q.infosec_exposure) || 0) + 25;
Q.news_headline =
    "A Telegram channel begins publishing the chancellery chief's private mail";
!}

= June 2021 — Published, unconfirmed, and probably real

A Telegram channel starts releasing the private mailbox of **Michał
Dworczyk**, head of the Prime Minister's chancellery. The material includes
draft government documents, pandemic decisions, appointment discussions and
correspondence with ministers, all of it conducted on private mail rather than
on the state system.

The government's response is the worst available one: it neither confirms nor
denies, warns that some material may be forged, and asks everyone to disregard
all of it. That answer guarantees that every genuine document is disputed and
every forged one is believed.

The security services describe the operation as consistent with Russian
activity. That is the part of the story most likely to be true and least likely
to be discussed, because both government and opposition have found more
immediately useful things to do with the contents.

[? if nik_referral_channel = 1: Our audit-chamber channel gives us a route to
examine the state's own information-security spending without touching a single
stolen file.?]
[? if procurement_scandal_stance = "Procurement standard": We already wrote one
transparency standard for this government last year, and it was ignored in
exactly the way this mailbox demonstrates.?]

- @dworczyk_infosec
- @dworczyk_use
- @dworczyk_refuse
- @dworczyk_committee

@dworczyk_infosec
title: Make it a state information-security failure, not a gossip file
subtitle: Ignores the contents entirely; the only route that survives being asked who benefits from the leak.
on-arrival: {!
Q.dworczyk_stance = "Information security";
Q.infosec_standard = 1;
Q.administrative_reform_pressure =
    (Number(Q.administrative_reform_pressure) || 0) + 5;
Q.institutional_trust = (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) + 5;
Q.security_incident_pressure =
    (Number(Q.security_incident_pressure) || 0) + 4;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 2;
Q.media_capacity = (Number(Q.media_capacity) || 0) + 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left treats the leak as a state security failure rather than a scandal";
!}

Our questions are about the system: why cabinet business was conducted on
consumer mail, which officials do the same, what the state's own rules require,
and who is responsible for enforcing them. We quote nothing from the channel.

It is a dull, disciplined position that costs us the entire news cycle. It is
also the only position that does not depend on the authenticity of documents
published by an actor whose interest in Polish politics is not our interest.

- @poland_hub: Continue

@dworczyk_use
title: Use the contents against the government
subtitle: Enormous short-term material; every future leak against anybody, including us, now has our precedent behind it.
on-arrival: {!
Q.dworczyk_stance = "Used the contents";
Q.media_capacity = (Number(Q.media_capacity) || 0) + 5;
Q.left_poll_momentum =
    (Number(Q.left_poll_momentum) || 0) + 0.2;
Q.pis_relation = (Number(Q.pis_relation) || 0) - 8;
Q.institutional_trust = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) - 5
);
Q.infosec_exposure =
    (Number(Q.infosec_exposure) || 0) + 10;
Q.russian_influence_salience = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.russian_influence_salience) || 0) - 4
);
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "Opposition deputies read the leaked chancellery correspondence into the record";
!}

The material is genuinely damning and we use it, page by page, in the chamber
and in the studios. The government cannot dispute a document without confirming
the rest of the mailbox.

We have also established, on the record, that stolen private correspondence is
legitimate parliamentary material when it is inconvenient for the right people.
There is no version of that rule that stays pointed away from us.

- @poland_hub: Continue

@dworczyk_refuse
title: Refuse to quote stolen material and say why in public
subtitle: Forfeits the story completely and buys a standard we can invoke when the target is ours.
on-arrival: {!
Q.dworczyk_stance = "Refused the material";
Q.institutional_trust = (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) + 6;
Q.constitutional_restraint =
    (Number(Q.constitutional_restraint) || 0) + 5;
Q.russian_influence_salience =
    (Number(Q.russian_influence_salience) || 0) + 5;
Q.media_capacity = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.media_capacity) || 0) - 2
);
Q.left_poll_momentum =
    (Number(Q.left_poll_momentum) || 0) - 0.1;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica declines to quote the hacked correspondence and explains the rule";
!}

We announce that our deputies will not read from the channel, and we say the
reason out loud: a foreign service selecting which Polish documents the public
sees is not a free press, and a parliament that treats its output as evidence
has outsourced its own agenda.

Journalists find it sanctimonious. It costs us a fortnight of coverage and
gains a position that will be worth a great deal on the day the same channel
starts publishing somebody on our side.

- @poland_hub: Continue

@dworczyk_committee
title: Convene a joint opposition information-security committee
subtitle: Requires working relations with KO. Builds a shared standard now that survives into government later.
choose-if: ko_relation >= 50
unavailable-subtitle: Relations with KO are too poor to convene anything jointly, and a one-party committee is a press release.
on-arrival: {!
Q.dworczyk_stance = "Joint opposition committee";
Q.infosec_standard = 1;
Q.opposition_infosec_committee = 1;
Q.ko_relation = (Number(Q.ko_relation) || 0) + 5;
Q.p2050_relation = (Number(Q.p2050_relation) || 0) + 3;
Q.institutional_trust = (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) + 5;
Q.administrative_reform_pressure =
    (Number(Q.administrative_reform_pressure) || 0) + 4;
Q.security_incident_pressure =
    (Number(Q.security_incident_pressure) || 0) + 3;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 3;
Q.news_headline =
    "The opposition parties agree one information-security standard between them";
!}

Three caucuses agree a single position: no quoting from the channel, one joint
demand for a state information-security review, and a written rule for what
each party does the next time a mailbox appears. It is the first thing this
opposition has agreed without a summit photograph.

The standard is small and it holds. When surveillance and hacking return to
Polish politics — and they return within six months — there is already a
document with three signatures on it, and none of the signatories has to invent
a position under pressure.

- @poland_hub: Continue
